  "configuration_id": "config_048",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_022 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.678), which clearly outperforms all other tested configurations. The RNA encoder scvi_n200 is the dominant factor (0.678 vs 0.639 for pca_n2000 vs 0.525 for scgpt), and avgpool+weighted is the preferred aggregation/fusion pair. The key untested dimension for the scvi_n200 pipeline is the image encoder: with pca_n2000, swapping resnet50→imagenet_vit_l was roughly neutral (0.639 vs 0.635), but the interaction with the more expressive scvi_n200 representation is unknown. Config_048 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) directly tests whether a stronger image encoder synergizes with the top RNA encoder while keeping the proven avgpool+weighted settings. This is the most logical single-step extension of the current best configuration and the highest-value use of experiment 7, leaving 3 experiments to further refine the winning recipe."
}

